  "slug": "scalable-commodity-1353",
  "summary": "Recent work pairs learned models with resolved readouts and adds genetic or mechanistic validation to neurodegeneration datasets.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is extracting disease-relevant structure from single-cell and proteomic data through interpretable computational frameworks. In Alzheimer's disease, the ADVISE preprint uses an explainable deep generative model to disentangle Braak-stage signals in snRNA-seq and prioritizes ROBO2, which is validated by CRISPRa. The published ADInteractome draws gene interactions from neural network internal states trained on snRNA-seq. NEPTUNE maps pathways from neuronal cell death markers derived from scRNA-seq differentially expressed gene lists. On the data side, a batch effect in the Answer ALS proteomic dataset (508 samples, 3,643 proteins) is corrected with ComBat using BDC controls. The newer element is coupling resolved readouts to experimental validation, while the ALS work addresses dataset reuse rather than mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
